    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7a7659ce-d5ff-5b37-99a3-f9534513c518",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=16 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-8.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-8)=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=8-(-8)=16.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=16$ and ${x}_{3}=-8$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(16)-(-8)=16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=16-(-16)-(8)=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=24$, ${x}_{2}=16$, and ${x}_{3}=-8.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨24,16,-8⟩.$",
