      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=17 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-9.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-9)=-8.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-8-(-9)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=-9$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)-(-9)=17.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=17-(-1)-(9)=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=9$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-9.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨9,1,-9⟩.\n$$",
